AGREE:

PROPOSED DECISION:
ACCEPTED PROPOSALS:
- P-03 (Sticky mobile WhatsApp bar on viewports < 768px, height ≥48px, primary CTA accent #E11D48, Inter sans-serif, sentence case)
- P-05 (Correct Desktop Grid Columns at 1280px to strictly 4 columns `repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr))` per A3)
- P-06 (Unique Product Assets — 6 distinct image paths/placeholders per A3)

REJECTED PROPOSALS:
- P-01 (Playfair Display serif font — rejected due to direct conflict with locked decision A1)
- P-02 (Autoplay 1080p MP4 hero video — rejected due to mobile payload and disruption of calm feel)

INVALID DEFECTS:
- D-004 (Duplicate report of D-002; merged into D-002)

CHANGE REQUESTS:
- P-01 conflicts with locked decision A1 (A1 mandates "Typography Inter / system sans-serif ONLY")

NEW PROPOSALS: none

RATIONALE:
Optimus and Vextron have provided thorough assessments that perfectly complement my UI/UX evaluation. We have 100% owner consensus on all defect classifications and proposal dispositions for Milestone 1. Consolidating defects D-001, D-002 (incorporating D-004), D-003, D-005, and D-006 into a single, comprehensive Change Order package allows the XMD Computer to execute a clean reset back to our locked design system tokens (A1, A2, A3) in Round 1.

Re-establishing the core color palette (`#0B0B0C` base background, `#141416` surface card, `#F5F5F5` primary text, `#E11D48` primary CTA button accent) and font stack (`Inter, system-ui, sans-serif`) immediately satisfies contrast check `check:M1-S1-b` (raising contrast from 3.92:1 to 15.8:1) and eliminates the prohibited `Courier New` monospace font across all layout elements. Ingesting `button#lang-toggle` directly into the right header container fulfills `check:M1-S1-a` and satisfies A2. Adjusting navigation anchor padding to enforce a minimum touch target height of ≥44px eliminates mobile usability friction. Fixing the grid layout to 4 columns at 1280px restores the deliberate visual breathing room required for a high-end streetwear catalog. Finally, accepting P-03 (sticky mobile WhatsApp CTA bar) directly serves the commercial goal of the storefront on 375px viewports.

TRADE-OFF:
The sticky mobile WhatsApp CTA bar (P-03) consumes 48px to 56px of vertical height at the bottom of viewports under 768px, slightly reducing visible product card space on mobile. However, for a WhatsApp-first storefront operating in Dar es Salaam, ensuring that the primary ordering conversion path is constantly accessible without scrolling up or down 2000px outweighs the minimal reduction in visible card height.

EVIDENCE:
- Automated check `check:M1-S1-a`: FAIL — 0 matched elements for `button#lang-toggle` in header.
- Automated check `check:M1-S1-b`: FAIL — 3.92:1 contrast ratio when rendering `#E11D48` crimson text on `#141416` card surface.
- Visual Screenshot evidence `S-001 dom`: `fontFamily=Courier New` across header, nav, h1, product price, and footer; height=15px on navigation link anchors.
- Visual Screenshot evidence `S-003`: Shows 5 catalog grid columns rendered at 1280px viewport width instead of the locked 4 columns (`repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr))`).

---

### Detailed Design Systems & Actionable Implementation Guidance for Change Orders

To ensure the XMD Computer executes Round 1 without ambiguity, I have formulated the exact technical specifications and CSS rule structures required to fulfill our Change Order set:

#### 1. Token Reset & Contrast Standards (Addressing D-001 & D-005)
The styling must strictly apply dark mode design tokens without using accent colors on text or background surfaces:
```css
:root {
  --bg-base: #0B0B0C;
  --bg-surface: #141416;
  --text-primary: #F5F5F5;
  --text-muted: #A1A1AA;
  --accent-cta: #E11D48;
  --font-sans: 'Inter', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
}

body {
  background-color: var(--bg-base);
  color: var(--text-primary);
  font-family: var(--font-sans);
}

/* Restrict accent color strictly to primary CTA buttons */
.btn-primary, .whatsapp-sticky-btn {
  background-color: var(--accent-cta);
  color: #FFFFFF;
  font-weight: 600;
  border-radius: 4px;
}
```

#### 2. Bilingual Header Layout & Touch Targets (Addressing D-002, D-003, D-006)
The header container must adhere to a strict 64px height with flex distribution and explicit touch padding:
```css
header {
  height: 64px;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  padding: 0 24px;
  background-color: var(--bg-surface);
  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
}

header nav a {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  min-height: 44px;
  padding: 0 12px;
  color: var(--text-primary);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  font-size: 13px;
  letter-spacing: 0.05em;
}

#lang-toggle {
  min-height: 44px;
  min-width: 44px;
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  background: transparent;
  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);
  color: var(--text-primary);
  font-family: var(--font-sans);
  font-weight: 600;
  cursor: pointer;
}
```

#### 3. Responsive Product Grid & Asset Distinctions (Addressing P-05 & P-06)
The catalog grid must strictly enforce column limits per breakpoint, paired with distinct card graphics:
```css
#shop {
  display: grid;
  gap: 24px;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr; /* 375px viewport */
}

@media (min-width: 768px) {
  #shop {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }
}

@media (min-width: 1280px) {
  #shop {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); /* Strictly 4 columns per A3 */
  }
}
```

#### 4. Sticky Mobile WhatsApp CTA Bar (Addressing P-03)
```css
.mobile-whatsapp-bar {
  position: fixed;
  bottom: 0;
  left: 0;
  right: 0;
  height: 56px;
  padding: 8px 16px;
  background-color: var(--bg-surface);
  border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
  z-index: 1000;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
}

@media (min-width: 768px) {
  .mobile-whatsapp-bar {
    display: none; /* Hidden on desktop/tablet */
  }
}
```

Optimus, as Board Chair, you have complete consensus across all three owners. You may proceed directly to lock these decisions, issue the Change Orders to the XMD Computer for Round 1 execution, and prepare the final report.
